    "tip": "Bases pair A–T and C–G, never A–G or C–T. Exams ask you to name the base that pairs with a given base and to write a complementary strand, so work through each letter in turn. For the diagram, draw the ladder straight, label both backbones and show hydrogen bonds between the bases. Don't add antiparallel strands or 3′ and 5′ ends: they are not asked."
