    "tip": "Students often write a prediction (“the mass will decrease”) when asked for a hypothesis, or a hypothesis with no reason. A hypothesis needs a reason (“because…”); a prediction says what will be observed. Never call a hypothesis an educated guess without adding that it is a testable explanation based on scientific knowledge."
