    "marks": 6,
    "model": "Transpiration is the loss of water vapour from the parts of a plant above the ground, mainly through the stomata of the leaves. It benefits the plant by pulling water and dissolved minerals up from the roots to the leaves in the transpiration stream. It also keeps the leaf cells turgid, so the leaves stay firm and spread out to the light, and evaporation cools the leaves in strong sunlight.",
    "prompt": "Define transpiration and state two ways in which it benefits a plant.",
    "type": "short"
