    "model": "Put the leaf-litter sample on a wire mesh (gauze) in a funnel. Place a lamp about 10–20 cm above the sample. Put a collecting beaker under the funnel, with damp tissue paper in it (or ethanol if the animals are to be preserved). Leave for several hours to a day. The heat and light from the lamp dry the sample from the top, so the animals move down away from the heat, light and dryness. They fall through the mesh into the beaker. The lamp drives the animals away from it; it does not attract them. The damp tissue keeps the animals alive in the beaker.",
    "prompt": "Describe how a Tullgren funnel is used to collect animals from leaf litter, and explain why the animals move into the collecting vessel.",
