    "prompt": "In a paternity case the mother’s bands at three loci are 8 and 11, 5 and 6, 14 and 17; the child’s are 11 and 12, 6 and 9, 14 and 15. Man P has 12 and 13, 9 and 9, 15 and 16. Man Q has 10 and 12, 7 and 9, 13 and 14. Which man could be the father? Explain.",
    "type": "short"
